 unless the recipients have the same licence with the NSRI as we do (which the Environment Agency has). If NRW has the same licence agreements as the EA that will be fine also. 3rd parties can not have the spatial data unless they have a licence with NSRI or pay NSRI for the use of your data. However they can view the data.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\tUnknown\tEditable\t2025-02-04T12:13:56.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n19712\tNRW_DS161313\tA survey to determine the status of the Depressed River Mussel Pseudanodonta complanata at eight monitoring stations within the River Wye (Lower Wye) SSSI in 2022\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313631333133\tData stored in the Welsh Invertebrate Database on Recorder6\tMichael Howe - Lead Specialist Advisor, Terrestrial Habitats and Species\t\t\tUnknown\tNon-editable\t2024-11-19T10:22:57.000Z\tJohn Beattie\t-\tPrivate record\n17627\tNRW_DS109818\tShellfish Stocks, Oystercatcher and Knot (bird) Modelling Data for the Burry Inlet and Three Rivers (2004-2007)\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313039383138\tAll the data is archived in project 158 and media no. 594. A copy is held on the MFSG shared drive with the report.\tInternal Contact: Senior Marine Monitoring Ecologist, MFSG Metadata contact: Data Services Team, NRW\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\tUnknown\tEditable\t2025-02-04T12:27:00.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\tMEDIN\tPublic record\n19044\tNRW_DS125331\tGenetic ancestry of introduced populations of sand lizard (Lacerta agilis) in Wales.\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313235333331\tData is held within science report 596 in NRW library - Data outputs associated with this project are archived in the Supercomputing Wales system “Hawk”, physically located at Cardiff University, with additional local back-up copies stored in the Environment Centre Wales, Bangor University on server–based storage at Natural Resources Wales.\tMatthew Ellis, Senior Advisor Casework Team NRW  Sam Dyer, Specialist advisor: Terrestrial habitats and s