ebrate Database stored on Recorder6\tMike Howe - Lead Specialist Advisor: Terrestrial Habitats and Species\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\tOpen Government Licence (OGL)\tUnknown\tNon-editable\t2025-02-04T12:43:26.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17784\tNRW_DS110509\tMonitoring and Surveillance of Special Areas of Conservation (SACs) in Wales\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313130353039\tMarine Monitoring is stored W: Drive  Terrestrial SAC Monitoring Paper Records: A filing cabinet of paper records which have not been digitised and is current stored with Tom Harrison.    Electronic Data: Our electronic data is stored in the following locations: Pre 2013 - On Ffynnon, SAC monitoring data is stored under the Monitoring folder for each SAC, e.g. Protected Sites - North Region - North West - Afon Gwyrfai a Llyn Cwellyn SAC ( SH55.11.100 ) – Monitoring Within each monitoring folder there will be a folder for each monitoring cycle of each feature, e.g. for the Gwyrfai there are folders for “Luronium natans 99 to 06”, “Luronium natans 07 to 12”, “Lutra lutra 99 to 06”, “Lutra Lutra 07 to 12”, etc.  There will also be a folder called “SAC Monitoring reports” which should contain the final SAC monitoring reports for each feature.  Post 2013 where projects were started once the DMS had been set up. This folder system is recreated on DMS for monitoring undertaken in the last 18 months or so.  It is all stored under the Land Management part of DMS: https://cyfoethnaturiolcymru.sharepoint.com/teams/landman/SitePages/Home.aspx\tInternal Custodians: North Region: Tom Harrison, Environmental Assessment Officer, NE EAAT. South Region: Karen Wilkinson, Environmental Assessment Officer, SE EAAT South Region: Dan Guest, Senior Environmental Assessment Officer, SW EAAT South Region: Alex Harding, Team Leader, SW EAAT Used to be: David Allen, Environmental Monitoring Manager, CCW  Metadata Contact: Data Services Team, NRW\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\tUnknown\tNon-editable\t2