t an update out of WISKI.\tNicola Wiltshire, Environmental Monitoring Officer 1, Rhymney \u0026amp; Ebbw A\u0026amp;R, NRW Mel Lacan, Senior Environmental Monitoring Officer, Rhymney \u0026amp; Ebbw A\u0026amp;R, NRW       Notes from 17/07/2018 The RHS data only currently goes up to 2014. When EAW split from EA we got an excel spreadsheet which contains the 1994 - 2004 data, extracted from EA\u0027s Ecosys module. This RHS acts as summary dataset, which is adequate for most people to use, and it includes indices of habitat type. This data is now stored in Keico (WISKI) which contains a lot of data from 2003 onwards. Pre 2003 the methodology was different so it has been hard to get the data into keico, Mel Lacan is hoping that by the end of the year, the data will be entered and they can start reporting again, therefore updating this dataset.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\tUnknown\tNon-editable\t2025-02-04T13:02:09.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n18578\tNRW_DS122202\tWales\u0027 grey seal photo-identification database: EIRPHOT (1992-2016)\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313232323032\tReports and outputs held in the DMS.  Database archived as project 480, media 1557.  Listed on the MS Access database plan to move to new NRW MS access storage/transactional area or MUP.\tTom Stringell, Senior Marine Mammal Ecologist\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\tValid\tEditable\t2025-02-04T10:02:19.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\tGEMINI \u0026 MEDIN\tPublic record\n17240\tEXT_DS121990\tWelsh Government: Technical Advice Note 8 (TAN8) Wind Energy Strategic Search Areas (3rd Party Data)\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313231393930\tX:\\Resource Management\\Welsh Government\\TAN8 Areas.lyr\tGIS and Spatial Data Team\tWelsh Government\t\tUnknown\tNon-editable\t2025-02-04T13:02:01.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n18106\tNRW_DS115575\tBangor University School of Ocean Science (SOS) Prince Madog Towed Video Survey of Caernarfon Bay (2013)\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-31313535