Biological\\Marine Habitat\\Fisheries habitat and sensitivity\\Intertidal sensitivity\\Severn Estuary.lyr\tInternal Custodian: Kirsten Ramsay, Team Leader, Marine \u0026amp; Coastal Ecosystems Team\t\t\tUnknown\tEditable\t2025-02-04T10:38:44.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n18623\tNRW_DS123236\tNRW Valleys Regional Park\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233323336\tx:\\Designations\\NRW Non-Statutory\\NRW Valleys Regional Park.lyr\tPeter Cloke\t\t\tUnknown\tEditable\t2025-02-04T10:30:27.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n17785\tNRW_DS110512\tMonitoring and Surveillance of National Nature Reserves (NNRs) in Wales\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313130353132\tIndividual NRW NNR warden offices. Data is fed into Countryside Monitoring System (CMS)  which is held on an external server accessed through a network connection. Contact Tom Hellewell about this.   The reserve staff and wardens hold a lot of the data - and also use a lot of the SAC and SSSI monitoring data to inform their site management plans.  September 2021 update - We still ask the NNR managers to update the data in CMSi. This was last done in November 2019. In the past we’ve tried to get it updated every 2 or 3 years – but looking to extend this to every 5 or 6 years as things really weren’t changing much. CMSi is good for at least another 2 years. There are plans to migrate the data to another system and the provisional plan was to do some development work on AMX to allow for this. However, this didn’t make the cut for this years IT development and no guarantee it will for next year either. Also not sure how this is affected by the AMX monitoring module – which I understand has been put on hold.\tInternal Custodian: Thomas Hellawell, Lead Specialist Advisor – Estates, Estate Planning Team Formerly David Allen, Environmental Monitoring \u0026amp; Surveillance, Monitoring \u0026amp; Surveillance Team\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\tUnknown\tNon-editable\t2025-02-04T12:56:08.000Z\tAstun Tec