er intranet and site files. This system has now been closed down and replaced by the protected sites management system. Currently there is no evidence \u0026amp; monitoring module on the system.\tInternal Custodian: Christine Edwards, Lead Specialist Advisor – Protected Sites programme       Metadata was archived 17th August 2021. Dylan Lloyd is the new custodian for this and has highlighted that after the ISIS System was decommissioned monitoring data was moved to the  protected sites baseline review data (124833) and will be used in the future possibly to populate a newer monitoring module when created.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\tUnknown\tEditable\t2025-02-04T12:56:31.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n17369\tNRW_DS24428\tLicencing held in the Integrated Sites Information System (ISIS) Database\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-3234343238\tISIS Database. Electronic. Available to NRW staff over intranet and site files.\tSpecies Protection Officer, Operational Support Group, NRW\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\tUnknown\tEditable\t2025-02-04T12:56:31.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17334\tNRW_DS24290\tPhoto Monitoring of Statutory Sites\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-3234323930\tSlides from photomonitoring pre-dating digital photography are archived in approximately 10 filling cabinets in NRW\u0027s archive (Bangor). Several plastic crates and carboard boxes of protected sites monitoring images in a store-room (F29) in Maes y Ffynnon\tInternal Custodian: Tom Harrison, Environmental Assessment Officer, NE EAAT.  (Originally managed by Stuart Matley, contact Monitoring Team, Operational Support Group, NRW)  Update from Tom Harrison 2021 - This dataset needs a custodian at a higher level to take responsibility for it.  Sarah Gorton has moved some of the images from the SSSI photomonitoring dataset from plastic crates into slide hangers in filing cabinets in Maes y Ffynnon.  These have been partly catalogued (to be completed post-COVID).  The other