0027s Advice:  This is a collection of images that was held by Linda Williams in CCW (also known as the CCW photo image library and identified as SOAP Ref: 003920 on the ETC).  All images are in the process of transferring to the NRW image library as part of the Image store project.  Have no idea about the hardcopy slides, which probably sit still in regional offices or have been transferred to Jill/Dwyn as part of office moves and paper archive project.  To be honest I am not sure that it needs an entry now as I don’t really consider promotional/nice images to be data and would just delete the entry. Alternatively perhaps change it for a general entry about the content of the NRW Image store in the same way we have a general entry for WISKI content or Marine Recorder content (it could include general information about the archive of slides that Jill/Dwyn currently hold too?).  Bryan Tozer would be best placed to help write a generic entry for the NRW image store (the lineage could include a sentence that described that this now contains what was previously knows as the CCW image library – a set of presentation level images used for promotional purposes). NRW holds so many images, unless they are a specifically data e.g. photo-monitoring time series of site/feature or something that is digitally analysed using software I wouldnt bother with metadata entries for them as they are not data and I don’t think they fall under our remit to give advice on.  If those that are considered data tend to be part of a larger dataset and are captures as part of the metadata for the larger dataset.\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\tUnknown\tEditable\t2025-02-04T12:59:33.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n17855\tNRW_DS111158\tMarine Nature Conservation Review Intertidal Survey of Rhos Point to New Brighton\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313131313538\tPaper report is available from NRW library, see \u0027related titles\u0027 field above. Data available on a copy of JNCC\u0027s