ata set here:- Z:\\Archive\\Legacy\\CCW_H_DRIVE\\Science\\TSG\\USERS\\RhindP\\Dune Spreadsheets.  According to Julie Creer this appears to be  \u0027Peter Rhind\u0027s own interrogation of the Phase 2 sand dune survey data (both the UK and Wales), which I suspect he got from the paper versions of survey. Looking at a few of the spreadsheets it looks like he separated out the different sand dune NVC communities and then tabulated which sites had those NVC communities and then added in the quadrat data tables for each site of that NVC type. S, in short, this is his analysis of that data and not the original dataset per se. These are most useful to me, but I’m not sure useful to anyone else?\u0027\tInternal Custodian: Julie Creer, Lead Specialist Advisor – Coastal Habitats, Marine \u0026amp; Coastal Ecosystems Team Metadata Contact: Data Services Team, NRW\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\tUnknown\tEditable\t2025-02-04T12:59:46.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\tMEDIN\tPublic record\n18761\tNRW_DS123378\tNRW Forest Soils\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333738\tx:\\Physical\\Soils\\NRW Forest Soil Map Coverage.lyr  x:\\Physical\\Soils\\NRW Forest Soils Line.lyr  x:\\Physical\\Soils\\NRW Forest Soils Point.lyr  x:\\Physical\\Soils\\NRW Forest Soils Polygon.lyr\t\t\t\tUnknown\tEditable\t2025-02-04T12:59:49.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n19085\tNRW_DS125370\tDevelopment and implementation of a monitoring project for two rare spiders (Heliophanus dampfi and Lasaeola prona) on bogs within Dyfi SSSI\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313235333730\tStored on the WID in Recorder 6\tMike Howe, Lead Specialist Advisor: Terrestrial Habitats and Species\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\tOpen Government Licence (OGL)\tUnknown\tEditable\t2025-02-04T12:39:48.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17284\tEXT_DS124289\tPublic rights of way (PROW) (3rd party data)\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234323839\tx:\\Recreation and Access\\Public rights of way\\PROW.lyr\tData Custodian: Ge