As) Biophysical Data Layer Project (3rd Party Data)\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313132343638\tArchived as Project 271, Media 983 and 1000-1013 (File paths - K:\\Archive\\Media 901to1000\\Media 983,  K:\\Archive\\Media 901to1000\\Media 1000, K:\\Archive\\Media 1001to1100\\Media 1001 etc etc.)  In addition to Related Titles: DCT-10-184068 Distribution of highly mobile species 2010 DCT-12-049886 Spawning and nursery grounds of selected fish species in UK waters 2012. DCT-10-075940 Oceanic thermal fronts from Earth observation data - a potential surrogate for pelagic diversity Summary Document 2010 DCT-10-184095 Development of marine diversity data layer: review of approaches and proposed methods 2009 DCT-10-077540 Residual current flow datalayer: Description of approach 2010 DCT-10-077274 Development of a Benthic Productivity Datalayer: Assessing the available approaches 2009 DCT-10-078178 Benthic productivity data layer development-North Sea Pilot Study 2010\tGIS Service Desk Internal Custodian: Kirsten Ramsay, Team Leader, Marine \u0026amp; Coastal Ecosystems Team (Formerly James Dargie who now works at NatureScot)        See Also: Report No 6, Task 1A. Report No 13, Task 1B. Report No 8, Task 2A. Report No 14, Task 2B. Report No17: Task 2D. Report No 24, Task 2i. Report No 22, Task 3.\tVarious-Department for Environment, Food and Rural Affairs (DEFRA)-Joint Nature Conservation Committee (JNCC)-Natural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\tUnknown\tNon-editable\t2025-02-04T12:00:18.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n18924\tNRW_DS124841\tFlood Risk Assessment Wales (FRAW)\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313234383431\tX\\Flood Risk\\Flood Risk Management\\Flood Risk Assessment Wales\tInternal Data Custodian(s): Mark Pugh (Flood Risk Analysis)  Metadata Point of Contact:  Mark Pugh, Simon James, Dave Tarrant (Flood Risk Analysis)\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\tOpen Government Licence\tValid\tNon-editable\t2025-02-04T10:22:50.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\tGEMINI\tPublic record\n18388\tNRW_DS119101\tMarine Special Area of Conservation (SAC) Features\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313139313031\tX:\\Biological\\Marine Habitat\\Marine SAC features\\SAC features X:\\Biological\\Marine Habitat\\Marine SAC features\\SAC Features Archive   There are 43 datasets\tKaren Robinson- Marine Ecologist - EVIAN       This metadata entry covers both the live data and the archive. Although current regulation is Reg 37, marine team have not updated any of the exiting layers.  Therefore the latest data is Reg 35 in the X drive data and is supplied in response to request for this dataset.  It is classed as Reg 37 data and a copy may be renamed to separate between the two.  Each layer will be updated as new evidence becomes available. The published data is technically the dataset generated for Reg35 but is the most recent information to inform Reg 37\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\tOpen Government Licence\tValid\tEditable\t2025-02-04T09:09:27.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\tGEMINI \u0026 MEDIN\tPublic record\n17080\tEXT_DS24275\tJNCC Conservation of River Macrophyte Database (3rd Party Data)\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-3234323735\tThe master version is available through the JNCC website http://jncc.defra.gov.uk/page-5815. NRW hold a copy in archive on server-based storage as project 293, media 1196.  This is the 2011 version, where restrictions were included and is an unreacted version. NRW have also downloaded a copy of the redacted version for general use\tSenior Freshwater Ecologist, Marine and Freshwater Evidence Group, NRW.  Tristan Hatton-Ellis acts as the data(base) manager for the Freshwater Lead Co-ordination Network, which represents JNCC on freshwater issues.   This responsibility may have been passed to Sue Hearn       JNCC have requested permission from all agencies/contributors to make this database available as open data 2016-05-11 (Lynn Heeley is main contact).  In principal NRW have agreed providing the database does not contain personal data or sensitive species.  When confirmed we will need to amend the metadata to OGL licences, requests would be referred to JNCC and we can add the correct resource locator.   Data was released under an OGL in 2016.  Personal data (recorder names) has been redacted.  Information about the original restrictions is held in the ReadMe file in the archive media 1196\tNatural England-Joint Nature Conservation Committee (JNCC)-Scottish Natural Heritage (SNH)-Natural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\tUnknown\tEditable\t2025-02-04T12:00:20.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17898\tNRW_DS111816\tMapping Marine Benthic Biodiversity in Wales\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313131383136\tThe data is archived as project 260, media no. 956 (File path is K:\\Archive\\Media 901to1000\\Media 956)\tInternal Custodian: Kirsten Ramsay, Team Leader, Marine \u0026amp; Coastal Ecosystems Team Metadata Point of Contact: Data Services, NRW\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\tUnknown\tEditable\t2025-02-04T11:49:32.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\tMEDIN\tPublic record\n17959\tNRW_DS114459\tIntertidal Monitoring of Eelgrass (Zostera marina) Beds in Pen Llyn a\u0027r Sarnau Special Areas of Conservation (SACs) 2010\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313134343539\tThe data and report are archived as Project No 199, Media No 1228. This archive is also maintained on backed-up server based storage at NRW, Maes y Fynnon\tInternal Custodian: Intertidal Ecologist, NRW Metadata contact: Master Reference Data Team\tNatural Resources Wales (NRW)\t\tUnknown\tEditable\t2025-02-04T12:00:17.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\tMEDIN\tPublic record\n17252\tEXT_DS123364\tForestry Commission Great Britain (FCGB) Forest Research Experiment Sites (3rd Party Data)\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313233333634\tx:\\Ownership\\Monitoring Equipment\\FCGB Forest Research Experiment Sites.lyr\tGeospatial Team, Knowledge Information Management\t\t\tUnknown\tEditable\t2025-02-04T10:45:24.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPrivate record\n17131\tEXT_DS120291\tAir Quality Co