es above for Seasearch reports available in NRW libraries.\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e           \u003c/nrw:internalLocationInfo\u003e           \u003cnrw:internalContactInfo\u003e             \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eGIS Service Desk Internal Custodian: Kirsten Ramsay, Team Leader, Marine \u0026amp; Coastal Ecosystems Team External Contacts: - Seasearch National Coordinator. chris@seasearch.org.uk. Marine Conservation Society, Unit 3 Wolf Business Park, Alton Road, Ross on Wye, Herefordshire, HR95NB - Liz Morris, North Wales Local Seasearch Organiser. liz@marine-ecosol.com - Kate Lock, West and South Wales Local Seasearch Organiser. rumbalock@tiscali.co.uk\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e           \u003c/nrw:internalContactInfo\u003e           \u003cnrw:relatedTitle\u003e             \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eGower seasearch 1995\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e           \u003c/nrw:relatedTitle\u003e           \u003cnrw:relatedTitle\u003e             \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eNorth Anglesey Seasearch survey\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e           \u003c/nrw:relatedTitle\u003e           \u003cnrw:relatedTitle\u003e             \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eNorth Pembrokeshire Seasearch Surveys 2002 - 04 : Summary Report\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e           \u003c/nrw:relatedTitle\u003e           \u003cnrw:relatedTitle\u003e             \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eNorth Wales Seasearch report 1995 - 1999\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e           \u003c/nrw:relatedTitle\u003e           \u003cnrw:relatedTitle\u003e             \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eSeasearch Stackpole Quay 1993 - 1998 : Summary\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e           \u003c/nrw:relatedTitle\u003e           \u003cnrw:relatedTitle\u003e             \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eSouth Wales Seasearch and fan shell survey June - August 2003\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e           \u003c/nrw:relatedTitle\u003e           \u003cnrw:relatedTitle\u003e             \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eStackpole Quay seasearch 1993 to 1998 : full report\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e           \u003c/nrw:relatedTitle\u003e         \u003c/nrw:MD_InternalInfo\u003e       \u003c/nrw:internalInfo\u003e     \u003c/nrw:MD_ContentInfo\u003e   \u003c/gmd:contentInfo\u003e   \u003cgmd:distributionInfo\u003e     \u003cgmd:MD_Distribution\u003e       \u003cgmd:distributionFormat\u003e         \u003cgmd:MD_Format\u003e           \u003cgmd:name gco:nilReason\u003d\"missing\"\u003e             \u003cgco:CharacterString /\u003e           \u003c/gmd:name\u003e           \u003cgmd:version gco:nilReason\u003d\"unknown\"\u003e             \u003cgco:CharacterString /\u003e           \u003c/gmd:version\u003e           \u003cgmd:specification gco:nilReason\u003d\"unknown\"\u003e             \u003cgco:CharacterString /\u003e           \u003c/gmd:specification\u003e         \u003c/gmd:MD_Format\u003e       \u003c/gmd:distributionFormat\u003e     \u003c/gmd:MD_Distribution\u003e   \u003c/gmd:distributionInfo\u003e   \u003cgmd:dataQualityInfo\u003e     \u003cgmd:DQ_DataQuality\u003e       \u003cgmd:scope\u003e         \u003cgmd:DQ_Scope\u003e           \u003cgmd:level\u003e             \u003cgmd:MD_ScopeCode codeList\u003d\"http://standards.iso.org/iso/19139/resources/gmxCodelists.xml#MD_ScopeCode\" codeListValue\u003d\"dataset\" /\u003e           \u003c/gmd:level\u003e         \u003c/gmd:DQ_Scope\u003e       \u003c/gmd:scope\u003e       \u003cgmd:report\u003e         \u003cgmd:DQ_DomainConsistency\u003e           \u003cgmd:result\u003e             \u003cgmd:DQ_ConformanceResult\u003e               \u003cgmd:specification\u003e                 \u003cgmd:CI_Citation\u003e                   \u003cgmd:title\u003e                     \u003cgmx:Anchor xlink:href\u003d\"http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2010/1089\"\u003eCommission Regulation (EU) No 1089/2010 of 23 November 2010 implementing Directive 2007/2/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council as regards interoperability of spatial data sets and services\u003c/gmx:Anchor\u003e                   \u003c/gmd:title\u003e                   \u003cgmd:date\u003e                     \u003cgmd:CI_Date\u003e                       \u003cgmd:date\u003e                         \u003cgco:Date\u003e2010-12-08\u003c/gco:Date\u003e                       \u003c/gmd:date\u003e                       \u003cgmd:dateType\u003e                         \u003cgmd:CI_DateTypeCode codeList\u003d\"http://standards.iso.org/iso/19139/resources/gmxCodelists.xml#CI_DateTypeCode\" codeListValue\u003d\"publication\" /\u003e                       \u003c/gmd:dateType\u003e                     \u003c/gmd:CI_Date\u003e                   \u003c/gmd:date\u003e                 \u003c/gmd:CI_Citation\u003e               \u003c/gmd:specification\u003e               \u003cgmd:explanation\u003e                 \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eThis dataset has not been assessed for conformance to the referenced INSPIRE regulation.\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e               \u003c/gmd:explanation\u003e               \u003cgmd:pass\u003e                 \u003cgco:Boolean\u003efalse\u003c/gco:Boolean\u003e               \u003c/gmd:pass\u003e             \u003c/gmd:DQ_ConformanceResult\u003e           \u003c/gmd:result\u003e         \u003c/gmd:DQ_DomainConsistency\u003e       \u003c/gmd:report\u003e       \u003cgmd:lineage\u003e         \u003cgmd:LI_Lineage\u003e           \u003cgmd:statement xsi:type\u003d\"gmd:PT_FreeText_PropertyType\"\u003e             \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eSeasearch divers use one of three tiers of recording. 1) The Seasearch Observation form is a straightforward form which is filled in with information about the main habitat and seabed cover types found on a dive and the main species of marine life encountered i.e. a single sample containing habitat and species data from each site. 2) The Seasearch Survey form is a more detailed account of a survey and includes species list using the SACFOR abundance scale, and habitat descriptions for each habitat found i.e. multiple habitat and species lists. 3) There are also a number of special projects with their own methodology e.g. Sea Fan Survey, Crawfish Survey and Skate and Ray Eggcase Survey. The recording forms from each of the above are handed in to the dive organiser or sent directly to Seasearch to be validated and entered into Marine Recorder. NRW holds a snapshot of all the surveys relating to Welsh coastal waters.\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e             \u003cgmd:PT_FreeText\u003e               \u003cgmd:textGroup\u003e                 \u003cgmd:LocalisedCharacterString locale\u003d\"#EN\"\u003eSeasearch divers use one of three tiers of recording. 1) The Seasearch Observation form is a straightforward form which is filled in with information about the main habitat and seabed cover types found on a dive and the main species of marine life encountered i.e. a single sample containing habitat and species data from each site. 2) The Seasearch Survey form is a more detailed account of a survey and includes species list using the SACFOR abundance scale, and habitat descriptions for each habitat found i.e. multiple habitat and species lists. 3) There are also a number of special projects with their own methodology e.g. Sea Fan Survey, Crawfish Survey and Skate and Ray Eggcase Survey. The recording forms from each of the above are handed in to the dive organiser or sent directly to Seasearch to be validated and entered into Marine Recorder. NRW holds a snapshot of all the surveys relating to Welsh coastal waters.\u003c/gmd:LocalisedCharacterString\u003e               \u003c/gmd:textGroup\u003e             \u003c/gmd:PT_FreeText\u003e           \u003c/gmd:statement\u003e         \u003c/gmd:LI_Lineage\u003e       \u003c/gmd:lineage\u003e     \u003c/gmd:DQ_DataQuality\u003e   \u003c/gmd:dataQualityInfo\u003e \u003c/gmd:MD_Metadata\u003e\tUnknown\tEditable\t2025-02-04T11:13:58.000Z\tAstun Technology Admi