rString\u003eHistoric Parks and Gardens - Walks Seating.LYR\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e           \u003c/gmd:alternateTitle\u003e           \u003cgmd:alternateTitle\u003e             \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eHistoric Parks and Gardens - Significant View.LYR\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e           \u003c/gmd:alternateTitle\u003e           \u003cgmd:alternateTitle\u003e             \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eHistoric Parks and Gardens - Gardens and Kitchen Gardens.LYR\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e           \u003c/gmd:alternateTitle\u003e           \u003cgmd:alternateTitle\u003e             \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eHistoric Parks and Gardens.LYR\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e           \u003c/gmd:alternateTitle\u003e           \u003cgmd:alternateTitle\u003e             \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eHistoric Parks \u0026amp; Gardens - Essential Setting.LYR\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e           \u003c/gmd:alternateTitle\u003e           \u003cgmd:alternateTitle\u003e             \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eParciau a Gerddi Hanesyddol (Data 3ydd Parti)\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e           \u003c/gmd:alternateTitle\u003e           \u003cgmd:date\u003e             \u003cgmd:CI_Date\u003e               \u003cgmd:date\u003e                 \u003cgco:Date\u003e2023-10-02\u003c/gco:Date\u003e               \u003c/gmd:date\u003e               \u003cgmd:dateType\u003e                 \u003cgmd:CI_DateTypeCode codeList\u003d\"http://standards.iso.org/iso/19139/resources/gmxCodelists.xml#CI_DateTypeCode\" codeListValue\u003d\"publication\" /\u003e               \u003c/gmd:dateType\u003e             \u003c/gmd:CI_Date\u003e           \u003c/gmd:date\u003e           \u003cgmd:identifier\u003e             \u003cgmd:MD_Identifier\u003e               \u003cgmd:code\u003e                 \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eEXT_DS111947\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e               \u003c/gmd:code\u003e             \u003c/gmd:MD_Identifier\u003e           \u003c/gmd:identifier\u003e         \u003c/gmd:CI_Citation\u003e       \u003c/gmd:citation\u003e       \u003cgmd:abstract xsi:type\u003d\"gmd:PT_FreeText_PropertyType\"\u003e         \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eThis is a third party spatial dataset owned by Cadw, who are the Welsh Governments historic environment services working for an accessible and well-protected historic environment for Wales. Wales has a rich inheritance of historic parks and gardens. They form an important and integral part of the historic and cultural fabric of the country.  Starting in 1992, CADW has undertaken a comprehensive survey of historic parks and gardens in Wales. Parks and gardens thought to be of national importance have been included in the Register of Parks and Gardens of Special Historic Interest in Wales and this dataset contains the digitised boundaries for the areas included in the Register.  The register was compiled in order to aid the informed conservation of historic parks and gardens by owners, local planning authorities, developers, statutory bodies and all concerned with them. This spatial dataset NRW has access to as part of the Historic parks and Gardens are as follows:  - Historic Parks and Gardens - Essential Setting - Historic Parks and Gardens - Historic Parks and Gardens - Gardens and Kitchen Gardens - Historic Parks and Gardens - Significant View - Historic Parks and Gardens - Walks Seating\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e         \u003cgmd:PT_FreeText\u003e           \u003cgmd:textGroup\u003e             \u003cgmd:LocalisedCharacterString locale\u003d\"#EN\"\u003eThis is a third party spatial dataset owned by Cadw, who are the Welsh Governments historic environment services working for an accessible and well-protected historic environment for Wales. Wales has a rich inheritance of historic parks and gardens. They form an important and integral part of the historic and cultural fabric of the country.  Starting in 1992, CADW has undertaken a comprehensive survey of historic parks and gardens in Wales. Parks and gardens thought to be of national importance have been included in the Register of Parks and Gardens of Special Historic Interest in Wales and this dataset contains the digitised boundaries for the areas included in the Register.  The register was compiled in order to aid the informed conservation of historic parks and gardens by owners, local planning authorities, developers, statutory bodies and all concerned with them. This spatial dataset NRW has access to as part of the Historic parks and Gardens are as follows:  - Historic Parks and Gardens - Essential Setting - Historic Parks and Gardens - Historic Parks and Gardens - Gardens and Kitchen Gardens - Historic Parks and Gardens - Significant View - Historic Parks and Gardens - Walks Seating\u003c/gmd:LocalisedCharacterString\u003e           \u003c/gmd:textGroup\u003e         \u003c/gmd:PT_FreeText\u003e       \u003c/gmd:abstract\u003e       \u003cgmd:pointOfContact\u003e         \u003cgmd:CI_ResponsibleParty\u003e           \u003cgmd:organisationName\u003e             \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eCadw. Welsh Historic Monuments\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e           \u003c/gmd:organisationName\u003e           \u003cgmd:contactInfo\u003e             \u003cgmd:CI_Contact\u003e               \u003cgmd:address\u003e                 \u003cgmd:CI_Address\u003e                   \u003cgmd:deliveryPoint\u003e                     \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eUnit 5/7 Cefn Coed, Parc Nantgarw, Cardiff, CF15 7Q, Wales\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e                   \u003c/gmd:deliveryPoint\u003e                   \u003cgmd:electronicMailAddress\u003e                     \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003ecadw@wales.gsi.gov.uk\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e                   \u003c/gmd:electronicMailAddress\u003e                 \u003c/gmd:CI_Address\u003e               \u003c/gmd:address\u003e               \u003cgmd:onlineResource\u003e                 \u003cgmd:CI