g\u003e     \u003c/gmd:PT_Locale\u003e   \u003c/gmd:locale\u003e   \u003cgmd:referenceSystemInfo\u003e     \u003cgmd:MD_ReferenceSystem\u003e       \u003cgmd:referenceSystemIdentifier\u003e         \u003cgmd:RS_Identifier\u003e           \u003cgmd:code\u003e             \u003cgmx:Anchor xlink:href\u003d\"http://www.opengis.net/def/crs/EPSG/0/27700\"\u003eBritish National Grid (EPSG::27700)\u003c/gmx:Anchor\u003e           \u003c/gmd:code\u003e         \u003c/gmd:RS_Identifier\u003e       \u003c/gmd:referenceSystemIdentifier\u003e     \u003c/gmd:MD_ReferenceSystem\u003e   \u003c/gmd:referenceSystemInfo\u003e   \u003cgmd:identificationInfo\u003e     \u003cgmd:MD_DataIdentification\u003e       \u003cgmd:citation\u003e         \u003cgmd:CI_Citation\u003e           \u003cgmd:title xsi:type\u003d\"gmd:PT_FreeText_PropertyType\"\u003e             \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eCadw: Listed Buildings (3rd Party Data)\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e             \u003cgmd:PT_FreeText\u003e               \u003cgmd:textGroup\u003e                 \u003cgmd:LocalisedCharacterString locale\u003d\"#EN\"\u003eCadw: Listed Buildings (3rd Party Data)\u003c/gmd:LocalisedCharacterString\u003e               \u003c/gmd:textGroup\u003e             \u003c/gmd:PT_FreeText\u003e           \u003c/gmd:title\u003e           \u003cgmd:alternateTitle\u003e             \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eListed Buildings.LYR\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e           \u003c/gmd:alternateTitle\u003e           \u003cgmd:alternateTitle\u003e             \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eAdeiladau Rhestredig Cadw (Data 3ydd Parti)\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e           \u003c/gmd:alternateTitle\u003e           \u003cgmd:date\u003e             \u003cgmd:CI_Date\u003e               \u003cgmd:date\u003e                 \u003cgco:Date\u003e2019-02-04\u003c/gco:Date\u003e               \u003c/gmd:date\u003e               \u003cgmd:dateType\u003e                 \u003cgmd:CI_DateTypeCode codeList\u003d\"http://standards.iso.org/iso/19139/resources/gmxCodelists.xml#CI_DateTypeCode\" codeListValue\u003d\"publication\" /\u003e               \u003c/gmd:dateType\u003e             \u003c/gmd:CI_Date\u003e           \u003c/gmd:date\u003e           \u003cgmd:identifier\u003e             \u003cgmd:MD_Identifier\u003e               \u003cgmd:code\u003e                 \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eEXT_DS111953\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e               \u003c/gmd:code\u003e             \u003c/gmd:MD_Identifier\u003e           \u003c/gmd:identifier\u003e         \u003c/gmd:CI_Citation\u003e       \u003c/gmd:citation\u003e       \u003cgmd:abstract xsi:type\u003d\"gmd:PT_FreeText_PropertyType\"\u003e         \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eNatural Resources of Wales (NRW) are supplied a number of historic and cultural datasets under a licence from Cadw. Cadw is the Welsh Government’s historic environment service working for an accessible and well-protected historic environment for Wales. They were set up with the aim of conserving Wales’s heritage, helping people understand and care about their history and helping to sustain the distinctive character of Wales.  Buildings and structures of national importance are given legal protection by being placed on a ‘List’ of Buildings of Special Architectural or Historic Interest. This is a third party spatial dataset containing information on the CADW designated sites and listed buildings in Wales. In Wales there are over 29,000 buildings and structures on the list. Listed buildings range from Medieval Churches to modern commercial premises etc, structures can include railings, gate piers, walls, war memorials, gravestones, post boxes and telephone boxes.\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e         \u003cgmd:PT_FreeText\u003e           \u003cgmd:textGroup\u003e             \u003cgmd:LocalisedCharacterString locale\u003d\"#EN\"\u003eNatural Resources of Wales (NRW) are supplied a number of historic and cultural datasets under a licence from Cadw. Cadw is the Welsh Government’s historic environment service working for an accessible and well-protected historic environment for Wales. They were set up with the aim of conserving Wales’s heritage, helping people understand and care about their history and helping to sustain the distinctive character of Wales.  Buildings and structures of national importance are given legal protection by being placed on a ‘List’ of Buildings of Special Architectural or Historic Interest. This is a third party spatial dataset containing information on the CADW designated sites and listed buildings in Wales. In Wales there are over 29,000 buildings and structures on the list. Listed buildings range from Medieval Churches to modern commercial premises etc, structures can include railings, gate piers, walls, war memorials, gravestones, post boxes and telephone boxes.\u003c/gmd:LocalisedCharacterString\u003e           \u003c/gmd:textGroup\u003e         \u003c/gmd:PT_FreeText\u003e       \u003c/gmd:abstract\u003e       \u003cgmd:pointOfContact\u003e         \u003cgmd:CI_ResponsibleParty\u003e           \u003cgmd:organisationName\u003e             \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eCadw. Welsh Historic Monuments\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e           \u003c/gmd:organisationName\u003e           \u003cgmd:contactInfo\u003e             \u003cgmd:CI_Contact\u003e               \u003cgmd:address\u003e                 \u003cgmd:CI_Address\u003e                   \u003cgmd:deliveryPoint\u003e                     \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eUnit 5/7 Cefn Coed, Parc Nantgarw, Cardiff, CF15 7Q, Wales\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e                   \u003c/gmd:deliveryPoint\u003e                   \u003cgmd:electronicMailAddress\u003e                     \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003ecadw@wales.gsi.gov.uk\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e                   \u003c/gmd:electronicMailAddress\u003e                 \u003c/gmd:CI_Address\u003e               \u003c/gmd:address\u003e               \u003cg