             \u003cgmd:date\u003e                         \u003cgco:Date\u003e2010-12-08\u003c/gco:Date\u003e                       \u003c/gmd:date\u003e                       \u003cgmd:dateType\u003e                         \u003cgmd:CI_DateTypeCode codeList\u003d\"http://standards.iso.org/iso/19139/resources/gmxCodelists.xml#CI_DateTypeCode\" codeListValue\u003d\"publication\" /\u003e                       \u003c/gmd:dateType\u003e                     \u003c/gmd:CI_Date\u003e                   \u003c/gmd:date\u003e                 \u003c/gmd:CI_Citation\u003e               \u003c/gmd:specification\u003e               \u003cgmd:explanation\u003e                 \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eThis dataset has not been assessed for conformance to the referenced INSPIRE regulation.\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e               \u003c/gmd:explanation\u003e               \u003cgmd:pass\u003e                 \u003cgco:Boolean\u003efalse\u003c/gco:Boolean\u003e               \u003c/gmd:pass\u003e             \u003c/gmd:DQ_ConformanceResult\u003e           \u003c/gmd:result\u003e         \u003c/gmd:DQ_DomainConsistency\u003e       \u003c/gmd:report\u003e       \u003cgmd:lineage\u003e         \u003cgmd:LI_Lineage\u003e           \u003cgmd:statement xsi:type\u003d\"gmd:PT_FreeText_PropertyType\"\u003e             \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eMultibeam echosounder onboard survey vessel. For full methodology refer to the IMAGIN report:  Kozachenko, M., Fletcher, R., Sutton, G., Monteys, X., Van Landeghem, K., Wheeler, A., Lassoued, Y., Cooper, A. and Nicoll, C. (2008) A geological appraisal of marine aggregate resources in the southern Irish Sea. Technical report produced for the Irish Sea Marine Aggregates Initiative (IMAGIN) project funded under the INTERREG IIIA Community Initiative Programme 2000-2006. University College Cork, Ireland, 390pp. ISBN 978-0-9556109-2-9. (see Record Number 09/26564 - IMAGIN).  Data confidence is high, as multibeam data will be positionally accurate. However due to problematic matching of survey lines and tide data - no tide gauge data was collected and the survey was not done to international hydrographic organization (IHO) standards.\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e             \u003cgmd:PT_FreeText\u003e               \u003cgmd:textGroup\u003e                 \u003cgmd:LocalisedCharacterString locale\u003d\"#EN\"\u003eMultibeam echosounder onboard survey vessel. For full methodology refer to the IMAGIN report:  Kozachenko, M., Fletcher, R., Sutton, G., Monteys, X., Van Landeghem, K., Wheeler, A., Lassoued, Y., Cooper, A. and Nicoll, C. (2008) A geological appraisal of marine aggregate resources in the southern Irish Sea. Technical report produced for the Irish Sea Marine Aggregates Initiative (IMAGIN) project funded under the INTERREG IIIA Community Initiative Programme 2000-2006. University College Cork, Ireland, 390pp. ISBN 978-0-9556109-2-9. (see Record Number 09/26564 - IMAGIN).  Data confidence is high, as multibeam data will be positionally accurate. However due to problematic matching of survey lines and tide data - no tide gauge data was collected and the survey was not done to international hydrographic organization (IHO) standards.\u003c/gmd:LocalisedCharacterString\u003e               \u003c/gmd:textGroup\u003e             \u003c/gmd:PT_FreeText\u003e           \u003c/gmd:statement\u003e         \u003c/gmd:LI_Lineage\u003e       \u003c/gmd:lineage\u003e     \u003c/gmd:DQ_DataQuality\u003e   \u003c/gmd:dataQualityInfo\u003e \u003c/gmd:MD_Metadata\u003e\tUnknown\tEditable\t2025-02-04T12:00:12.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17084\tEXT_DS114968\tBangor University Acoustic Multibeam Echosounder Survey of the North Llyn Modiolus Bed 2008 (3rd Party Data)\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313134393638\tArchived as Project 234, Media 1354,1355,1356.   Raw data is stored at the School of Ocean Sciences, Bangor University\tGIS Service Desk  Subtidal Team, MFEG, NRW External Custodian:  Dr. Jim Burnell (Experimental Physicist), Ocean Sciences, Craig Mair Building, Bangor University The data was then processed by Christian Wilson at CEFAS\t\u003cgmd:MD_Metadata xmlns:gmd\u003d\"http://www.isotc211.org/2005/gmd\" xmlns:xsi\u003d\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\" xmlns:gco\u003d\"http://www.isotc211.org/2005/gco\" xmlns:srv\u003d\"http://www.isotc211.org/2005/srv\" xmlns:gmx\u003d\"http://www.isotc211.org/2005/gmx\" xmlns:gts\u003d\"http://www.isotc211.org/2005/gts\" xmlns:gsr\u003d\"http://www.isotc211.org/2005/gsr\" xmlns:gmi\u003d\"http://www.isotc211.org/2005/gmi\" xmlns:gss\u003d\"http://www.isotc211.org/2005/gss\" xmlns:nrw\u003d\"http://naturalresources.wales/nrw\" xmlns:gml\u003d\"http://www.opengis.net/gml/3.2\" xmlns:xlink\u003d\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"\u003e   \u003cgmd:fileIdentifier\u003e     \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003e4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313134393638\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e   \u003c/gmd:fileIdentifier\u003e   \u003cgmd:language\u003e     \u003cgmd:LanguageCode codeList\u003d\"http://www.loc.gov/standards/iso639-2/\" codeListValue\u003d\"eng\"\u003eEnglish\u003c/gmd:LanguageCode\u003e   \u003c/gmd:language\u003e   \u003cgmd:parentIdentifier\u003e     \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eNRW_DS109891\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e   \u003c/gmd:parentIdentifier\u003e   \u003cgmd:hierarchyLevel\u003e     \u003cgmd:MD_ScopeCode codeList\u003d\"http://standards.iso.org/iso/19139/resources/gmxCodelists.xml#MD_ScopeCode\" codeListValue\u003d\"dataset\" /\u003e   \u003c/gmd:hierarchyLevel\u003e   \u003cgmd:contact\u003e     \u003cgmd:CI_ResponsibleParty\u003e       \u003cgmd:organisationName gco:nilReason\u003d\"missing\"\u003e         \u003cgco:CharacterString /\u003e       \u003c/gmd:organisationName\u003e       \u003cgmd:contactInfo\u003e         \u003cgmd:CI_Contact\u003e           \u003cgmd:address\u003e             \u003cgmd:CI_Address\u003e               \u003cgmd:deliveryPoint gco:nilReason\u003d\"missing\"\u003e    