ssions for use\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e           \u003c/nrw:internalLocationInfo\u003e           \u003cnrw:internalContactInfo\u003e             \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eInternal Custodian: Kirsten Ramsay, Team Leader, Marine \u0026amp; Coastal Ecosystems Team GIS Service Desk  External Custodian: EirGrid Plc\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e           \u003c/nrw:internalContactInfo\u003e           \u003cnrw:relatedTitle gco:nilReason\u003d\"missing\"\u003e             \u003cgco:CharacterString /\u003e           \u003c/nrw:relatedTitle\u003e         \u003c/nrw:MD_InternalInfo\u003e       \u003c/nrw:internalInfo\u003e     \u003c/nrw:MD_ContentInfo\u003e   \u003c/gmd:contentInfo\u003e   \u003cgmd:distributionInfo\u003e     \u003cgmd:MD_Distribution\u003e       \u003cgmd:distributionFormat\u003e         \u003cgmd:MD_Format\u003e           \u003cgmd:name\u003e             \u003cgmx:Anchor xlink:href\u003d\"http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/M01/current/DOC\"\u003eDocuments\u003c/gmx:Anchor\u003e           \u003c/gmd:name\u003e           \u003cgmd:version gco:nilReason\u003d\"unknown\" /\u003e           \u003cgmd:specification\u003e             \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003e[A] Reports and appendices in .pdf format [B] Report Images/charts for each of the above [C] GIS data in ArcView and for use with ERMapper. Include habitat data (grab Photo locations, contours, seabed photo locations, side Scan locations, Video footage locations) [D] SideScan images in GeoTiff format [E] Source data.  unprocessed XYZ data for Bathymetry and sidescan data. [F] Processed gridded xyz data in tiff form [G] Images of sediment grabs and seabed [H] Video data in .VOB format (for use with DVD) [I] Supporting information as txt and pdf files.  Information about data and permissions for use\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e           \u003c/gmd:specification\u003e         \u003c/gmd:MD_Format\u003e       \u003c/gmd:distributionFormat\u003e     \u003c/gmd:MD_Distribution\u003e   \u003c/gmd:distributionInfo\u003e   \u003cgmd:dataQualityInfo\u003e     \u003cgmd:DQ_DataQuality\u003e       \u003cgmd:scope\u003e         \u003cgmd:DQ_Scope\u003e           \u003cgmd:level\u003e             \u003cgmd:MD_ScopeCode codeList\u003d\"http://standards.iso.org/iso/19139/resources/gmxCodelists.xml#MD_ScopeCode\" codeListValue\u003d\"dataset\" /\u003e           \u003c/gmd:level\u003e         \u003c/gmd:DQ_Scope\u003e       \u003c/gmd:scope\u003e       \u003cgmd:report\u003e         \u003cgmd:DQ_DomainConsistency\u003e           \u003cgmd:result\u003e             \u003cgmd:DQ_ConformanceResult\u003e               \u003cgmd:specification\u003e                 \u003cgmd:CI_Citation\u003e                   \u003cgmd:title\u003e                     \u003cgmx:Anchor xlink:href\u003d\"http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2010/1089\"\u003eCommission Regulation (EU) No 1089/2010 of 23 November 2010 implementing Directive 2007/2/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council as regards interoperability of spatial data sets and services\u003c/gmx:Anchor\u003e                   \u003c/gmd:title\u003e                   \u003cgmd:date\u003e                     \u003cgmd:CI_Date\u003e                       \u003cgmd:date\u003e                         \u003cgco:Date\u003e2010-12-08\u003c/gco:Date\u003e                       \u003c/gmd:date\u003e                       \u003cgmd:dateType\u003e                         \u003cgmd:CI_DateTypeCode codeList\u003d\"http://standards.iso.org/iso/19139/resources/gmxCodelists.xml#CI_DateTypeCode\" codeListValue\u003d\"publication\" /\u003e                       \u003c/gmd:dateType\u003e                     \u003c/gmd:CI_Date\u003e                   \u003c/gmd:date\u003e                 \u003c/gmd:CI_Citation\u003e               \u003c/gmd:specification\u003e               \u003cgmd:explanation\u003e                 \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eThis dataset has not been assessed for conformance to the referenced INSPIRE regulation.\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e               \u003c/gmd:explanation\u003e               \u003cgmd:pass\u003e                 \u003cgco:Boolean\u003efalse\u003c/gco:Boolean\u003e               \u003c/gmd:pass\u003e             \u003c/gmd:DQ_ConformanceResult\u003e           \u003c/gmd:result\u003e         \u003c/gmd:DQ_DomainConsistency\u003e       \u003c/gmd:report\u003e       \u003cgmd:lineage\u003e         \u003cgmd:LI_Lineage\u003e           \u003cgmd:statement xsi:type\u003d\"gmd:PT_FreeText_PropertyType\"\u003e             \u003cgco:CharacterString\u003eGeophysical survey used single and multibeam echosounder, sidescan sonar, gradiometer and sub-bottom profiler / boomer.  Additional multibeam and echosounder lines were surveyed to the south of the original proposed route between approximately KP 111 and KP 117, of the surveyed route, to investigate an area of horse mussels (Modiolus modiolus).  Environmental survey involved sediment sampling and drop-down digital still and video photography at 110 stations. Grab sampling using a 0.1 m2 Day grab or 0.1 m2 Hamon grab was undertaken at 110 stations with each retained sample photographed and logged to provide a description of the sediment and any obvious fauna. Towed camera transects were undertaken along selected regions of the route corridor using a Kongsberg oe14-208 digital stills camera with video streaming capability. Bathymetry survey all water depths were reduced to Lowest Astronomical Tide (LAT). Positions are described relative to the surveyed cable route The survey was contracted by EirGrid (State owned power transmission company, that owns and operates the Irish National electricity grid) High - all observations made by experienced proffesional contractors following international standards and methodology of data collection.\u003c/gco:CharacterString\u003e             \u003cgmd:PT_FreeText\u003e               \u003cgmd:textGroup\u003e                 \u003cgmd:LocalisedCharacterString locale\u003d\"#EN\"\u003eGeophysical survey used single and multibeam echosounder, sidescan sonar, gradiometer and sub-bottom profiler / boomer.  Additional multibeam and echosounder lines were surveyed to the south of the original proposed route between approximately KP 111 and KP 117, of the surveyed route, to investigate an area of horse mussels (Modiolus modiolus).  Environmental survey involved sediment sampling and drop-down digital still and video photography at 110 stations. Grab sampling using a 0.1 m2 Day grab or 0.1 m2 Hamon grab was undertaken at 110 stations with each retained sample photographed and logged to provide a description of the sediment and any obvious fauna. Towed camera transects were undertaken along selected regions of the route corridor using a Kongsberg oe14-208 digital stills camera with video streaming capability. Bathymetry survey all water depths were reduced to Lowest Astronomical Tide (LAT). Positions are described relative to the surveyed cable route The survey was contracted by EirGrid (State owned power transmission company, that owns and operates the Irish National electricity grid) High - all observations made by experienced proffesional contractors following international standards and methodology of data collection.\u003c/gmd:LocalisedCharacterString\u003e               \u003c/gmd:textGroup\u003e             \u003c/gmd:PT_FreeText\u003e           \u003c/gmd:statement\u003e         \u003c/gmd:LI_Lineage\u003e       \u003c/gmd:lineage\u003e     \u003c/gmd:DQ_DataQuality\u003e   \u003c/gmd:dataQualityInfo\u003e \u003c/gmd:MD_Metadata\u003e\tUnknown\tNon-editable\t2025-02-04T12:00:15.000Z\tAstun Technology Admin\t-\tPublic record\n17129\tEXT_DS115167\tJNCC Acoustic Multibeam Echosounder Survey of two sites off North West Anglesey 2009 (3rd Party Data)\t4f4c4942-4343-5764-6473-313135313637\tArchived as Project 381, Media 1392. Subsequent drop down video surveys carried out in the same areas are: Archived as Project 268, Media 1309.\tGIS Service Desk  Extern